      "group_id": 101010102,
      "name": "Length of Peak Period",
      "position": 5,
      "guide": "Length of Peak Period(s)\n\n* Helps determine peak/non - peak volumes and speeds for emissions and operating cost benefit calculations.\n* Insert the number of peak period hours per typical day. Default is 5 hours (statewide avg).\n* This model estimates total % daily traffic occurring during peak period using a lookup table developed from Traffic Census data. No difference between weekdays and weekends.\n\nExamples:\n* If peak period is four hours from 3PM to 7PM, then enter a “4”.\n* To model a 24-hour HOV or HOT lane, enter 24 hours so peak is 100% of average daily traffic.\n* To model a ramp metering project, enter the hours per day that metering is operational."
